<reference id="scenario_profiling_in_practice" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario: profiling in practice</title>
   <shortdesc>When publishing for Windows users, only the Windows step appears.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>platform</keyword>
        <keyword>Scenario</keyword>
        <keyword>profiling</keyword>
        <keyword>practice</keyword>
        <keyword>Windows</keyword>
        <keyword>appears</keyword>
        <indexterm>platform</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Scenario</indexterm>
        <indexterm>profiling</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody><section>
      <p>When publishing for Windows users, only the Windows step appears. The admin-specific post-requisite appears only in administrator documentation.</p>
      <codeblock>&lt;task id="t_install"&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Install the Application&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;taskbody&gt;
&lt;steps&gt;
&lt;step platform="windows"&gt;
&lt;cmd&gt;Double-click &lt;filepath&gt;setup.exe&lt;/filepath&gt;.&lt;/cmd&gt;
&lt;/step&gt;
&lt;step platform="linux"&gt;
&lt;cmd&gt;Run &lt;codeph&gt;sudo ./install.sh&lt;/codeph&gt;.&lt;/cmd&gt;
&lt;/step&gt;
&lt;step platform="macos"&gt;
&lt;cmd&gt;Drag the application to &lt;filepath&gt;Applications&lt;/filepath&gt;.&lt;/cmd&gt;
&lt;/step&gt;
&lt;step&gt;
&lt;cmd&gt;Follow the on-screen instructions.&lt;/cmd&gt;
&lt;/step&gt;
&lt;/steps&gt;
&lt;postreq audience="admin"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Configure server settings. See &lt;xref href="t_configure_server.dita"/&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/postreq&gt;
&lt;/taskbody&gt;
&lt;/task&gt;</codeblock>
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
      
